    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, but **not with temperature 0**: this SDK version doesn't allow it.\n\n**Why no temperature:** in the pinned `anthropic==1.8.0`, `Messages.create()` no longer has `temperature`, `top_k` or `top_p` parameters. The project's CLAUDE.md says this too, and I confirmed it in the installed SDK (`.venv/.../resources/messages/messages.py:117`). I could have forced it in through `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`, but that goes around a parameter the SDK removed on purpose and the API may reject the request. I also couldn't upgrade or downgrade, since the project forbids changing pinned versions.\n\n**What it does:**\n- Sends one `client.messages.create` call to `MODEL` with `max_tokens=5`.\n- The system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from `bug, feature, question`, and the ticket text goes in as the user message.\n- It joins the text of the reply, strips it and lower-cases it, and returns `\"question\"` if the result isn't in `LABELS`.\n\n**What this means for determinism:** the output is always one of the three labels. But without temperature 0 I can't promise the same ticket always gets the same label. If that's a firm requirement, you could:\n1. Accept this, since a short, tightly constrained answer is usually stable in practice.\n2. Try `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`, if you know the API still accepts it for `claude-sonnet-4-6`. I haven't checked this.\n3. Cache labels by ticket text so a repeated ticket always gets the same label.\n\n**Tests:** `pytest -q` passes, but it's only the one existing test, which checks that `LABELS` are lower-case. Nothing calls `label_ticket`, and I haven't tested it against the live API."
  },
